"login":"charettes","id":9293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes","html_url":"https://github.com/charettes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-01-14T23:25:21Z","updated_at":"2019-01-14T23:25:21Z","body":"Thanks for the tweaks and merge @timgraham.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/454202757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465242160","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/10840#issuecomment-465242160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/10840","id":465242160,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NTI0MjE2MA==","user":{"login":"bluetech","id":1223550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjM1NTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1223550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech","html_url":"https://github.com/bluetech","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-19T18:00:06Z","updated_at":"2019-02-19T18:00:06Z","body":"@charettes Regarding the commit \"Prevented timezone assignment for unusable PostgreSQL connections.\".\r\n\r\nWe've recently switched from using Django's persistent connections to using an external connection pool, pgbouncer. This means each request creates a new connection, and so I looked at reducing connection startup latency as much as possible (on the Django side, pgbouncer itself is pretty fast). The major latency contribution I noticed was the `ensure_timezone` function - turns out our application and the DB didn't agree on the value so the `cursor.execute(self.ops.set_time_zone_sql(), [timezone_name])` code path was taken, which adds a DB roundtrip. We fixed this misconfiguration and that helped.\r\n\r\nThis commit adds an unconditional roundtrip to the same function. So this will be a slight performance regression for us.\r\n\r\nDo you think this can use a \"better ask for forgiveness\" approach (try and catch the exception) instead, to avoid the roundtrip in the happy path?\r\n\r\n(As a side note, it seems odd that a check if a connection is usable is needed when the connection was just obtained a couple lines before, but I didn't dig into the actual problem being fixed.)\r\n\r\nThanks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465242160/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465248303","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/10840#issuecomment-465248303","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/10840","id":465248303,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NTI0ODMwMw==","user":{"login":"charettes","id":9293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes","html_url":"https://github.com/charettes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-19T18:16:30Z","updated_at":"2019-02-19T18:16:30Z","body":"Hello @bluetech,\r\n\r\n> The major latency contribution I noticed was the `ensure_timezone` function - turns out our application and the DB didn't agree on the value so the `cursor.execute(self.ops.set_time_zone_sql(), [timezone_name])` code path was taken, which adds a DB roundtrip. We fixed this misconfiguration and that helped.\r\n\r\nSorry for all the trouble here but [this is documented behaviour](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/2.1/ref/databases/#optimizing-postgresql-s-configuration).\r\n\r\n> This commit adds an unconditional roundtrip to the same function. So this will be a slight performance regression for us.\r\n>\r\n> Do you think this can use a \"better ask for forgiveness\" approach (try and catch the exception) instead, to avoid the roundtrip in the happy path?\r\n> \r\n> (As a side note, it seems odd that a check if a connection is usable is needed when the connection was just obtained a couple lines before, but I didn't dig into the actual problem being fixed.)\r\n\r\nRight, I assume `ensure_timezone` could accept an `ensure_usable=True` kwarg to avoid the `if not self.is_usable`.\r\n\r\nCould you file a ticket and submit a PR to address it?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465248303/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465274361","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/10840#issuecomment-465274361","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/10840","id":465274361,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NTI3NDM2MQ==","user":{"login":"charettes","id":9293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes","html_url":"https://github.com/charettes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-19T19:23:55Z","updated_at":"2019-02-19T19:23:55Z","body":"@bluetech, [submited a ticket](https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/30193#ticket) and currently working on a fix.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465274361/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465300352","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/10840#issuecomment-465300352","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/10840","id":465300352,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ2NTMwMDM1Mg==","user":{"login":"bluetech","id":1223550,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjM1NTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1223550?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech","html_url":"https://github.com/bluetech","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluetech/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-02-19T20:38:40Z","updated_at":"2019-02-19T20:38:40Z","body":"> Sorry for all the trouble here but [this is documented behaviour](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/2.1/ref/databases/#optimizing-postgresql-s-configuration).\r\n\r\nYes, this was definitely a misconfiguration on our part. Thanks for the reference.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/465300352/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]